{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-checked answer keys for the corpus tasks: the files that actually",
    "implement or test the behaviour each task names, read out of each project",
    "at the commit pinned in corpus.example.json.",
    "",
    "`group` is the honest part. The six 'tuned' repositories were used while",
    "tuning ranking constants (RELATIONSHIP_BONUS, HISTORY_DOC_PENALTY,",
    "DISCOVERY_LIMIT), so results on them are fitted to some unknown degree.",
    "The four 'held_out' keys were written before OpenContextually was ever",
    "run against those repositories on these tasks, and nothing was tuned",
    "afterwards. Quote both numbers or neither.",
    "",
    "A key lists what a developer would need open to fix the thing, not every",
    "file that mentions it: the implementation, the dependency the fix reaches",
    "through, the configuration contract where there is one, and the test.",
    "",
    "The 'held_out_2' group is a second reserved set, added after the first held-out run exposed the duplicate-copy failure class. Their keys were written and committed before the fix for that class existed, so they measure whether it generalizes rather than whether it was fitted."
  ],
